<item><title>Naira firms slightly in official market as parallel rate stays above N1,440</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/naira-firms-slightly-in-official-market-as-parallel-rate-a5acfb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/naira-firms-slightly-in-official-market-as-parallel-rate-a5acfb/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The official interbank rate stood at N1,350.50 to the dollar early on Thursday, while street dealers in Lagos and Abuja quoted between N1,445 and N1,468.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:54:14 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/naira-firms-slightly-in-official-market-as-parallel-rate-a5acfb/share.jpg" length="42159" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/naira-firms-slightly-in-official-market-as-parallel-rate-a5acfb/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
